// TNG THEATERS - who a mission fights, and in what proportion.
//
// THESE USED TO BE ALIASES. Every theater in this file rostered the same four stock names -
// `kralien, torgoth, arvonian, ximni` - and differed only in an `Art:` map saying what those
// races should LOOK like. It had to: LegendaryMissions branched on the race name to pick an
// enemy station type, so a roster naming Trek factions made every branch fall through and
// the map spawned no enemy stations at all, silently.
//
// It does not any more. A race is a shipData `origin`, so the seven factions this pack
// already ships ARE races the moment their hulls load - `race_station_hull("cardassian")`
// answers `tng_crd_terok_nor` because that is the Cardassian hull carrying the `station`
// role. So these roster Trek factions outright, and the consequences are worth naming:
//
//   * A THEATER IS NO LONGER FOUR LONG. The old weight table was four columns wide, so a
//     roster was four long. Weights are keyed by race now, so a theater fields as many
//     factions as it likes - and CAN MIX, which was previously unspellable because
//     `kralien` was simultaneously a slot name and a real race.
//   * `Art:` KEEPS ONLY THE FRIENDLY RE-SKIN. The enemy entries are gone because there is
//     nothing left to re-skin: a Cardassian spawns a Cardassian hull directly. What remains
//     is `usfp`, `tsn` and `civ`, which are not enemies - they dress the friendly side, and
//     `usfp` is the one that is easy to miss, because stock starbases and civilian
//     freighters are side `USFP` and NOT `tsn`.
//   * KLINGONS AND ORIONS HAVE NO STARBASE in this pack, and neither does the Breen. The
//     maps that build enemy stations filter on `race_has_station`, so those factions simply
//     do not turn up as station-holders in borderwar and deepstrike while still raiding
//     everywhere else. Nothing needs saying here for that to work.
//
// WHAT THE LADDER MEANS. One faction dominates at low difficulty and the mix diversifies as
// it hardens. Whoever is written at the top weight is the faction a low-difficulty night is
// mostly about - which used to be decided by whichever race the hull pairing happened to put
// in the 70% slot, i.e. by nobody.
//
// FACTION DEPTH STILL DECIDES WHAT CAN LEAD. Cardassian, Klingon, Romulan, Kazon and Orion
// field four hulls each; Dominion two; Breen exactly ONE. A faction leading with one hull
// means every enemy that night is the same model, so Breen and Dominion are only ever given
// small shares. `theater_depth_report()` enforces this and names the faction if it is got
// wrong.

# [Dominion War](dominion_war)
---
Weights 1:  cardassian:85, dominion:5,  breen:4,  klingon:6
Weights 5:  cardassian:70, dominion:10, breen:8,  klingon:12
Weights 11: cardassian:34, dominion:22, breen:14, klingon:30
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: dominion=jemhadar, breen=vorta, tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
The Alpha Quadrant at war. Cardassian space is the front line, the Dominion holds the
wormhole, and a Breen raid is the thing nobody is ready for. Matches the Chin'toka and DS9
trials, so it is the theater to run alongside them.

# [Klingon War](klingon_war)
---
Weights 1:  klingon:85, romulan:5,  orion:5,  kazon:5
Weights 5:  klingon:70, romulan:10, orion:10, kazon:10
Weights 11: klingon:10, romulan:30, orion:30, kazon:30
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
The alliance has broken. Every faction here has four hulls, which makes this the most varied
theater in the pack - the one to pick if a night should not feel repetitive.

# [Romulan Cold War](romulan_cold_war)
---
Weights 1:  romulan:85, klingon:5,  cardassian:5,  orion:5
Weights 5:  romulan:70, klingon:10, cardassian:10, orion:10
Weights 11: romulan:10, klingon:30, cardassian:30, orion:30
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
Warbirds decloaking on the Neutral Zone. Klingons and Cardassians circle the edges, and the
Orions take what is left unattended.

# [Delta Quadrant](delta_quadrant)
---
Weights 1:  kazon:85, romulan:5,  cardassian:5,  klingon:5
Weights 5:  kazon:70, romulan:10, cardassian:10, klingon:10
Weights 11: kazon:10, romulan:30, cardassian:30, klingon:30
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
Kazon sects everywhere and a long way from home. This is what the conversion produced by
ACCIDENT before theaters existed - the hull pairing put Kazon in the 70% slot - so it is
kept, and named, because it is a perfectly good theater once it is a choice.

# [Orion Syndicate](orion_syndicate)
---
Weights 1:  klingon:85, cardassian:5,  breen:5,  romulan:5
Weights 5:  klingon:70, cardassian:10, breen:8,  romulan:12
Weights 11: klingon:10, cardassian:30, breen:20, romulan:40
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: breen=vorta, tsn=orion, civ=human
Music: TNG_Music
Player Faction: Orion
Player Side Name: Orion Syndicate
Player Side Color: #fa0
Player Side Icon: 7
---
The crew are pirates. This is the theater that shows what the player fields are for: the
crew fly Orion hulls under Orion colors with Orion faces, while their `tsn` ALLIES stay
Federation - two different things the one word "tsn" used to decide.

Nothing here moves a side KEY. The crew are still side `tsn` to the engine, so every
relation, every `//comms` gate and every friendly starbase behaves exactly as the mission
wrote it. Only the costume changed. `Player Side Key:` would make them genuinely hostile
and is refused, loudly, until the missions stop hardcoding `tsn`.

# [Border Skirmish](border_skirmish)
---
Weights 1:  cardassian:60, kralien:20, klingon:10, torgoth:10
Weights 5:  cardassian:40, kralien:25, klingon:20, torgoth:15
Weights 11: cardassian:25, kralien:25, klingon:25, torgoth:25
Art:   usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
THE ONE THAT WAS IMPOSSIBLE BEFORE. Trek factions and stock Artemis factions in the same
roster, each flying its own hulls with its own fleet ladder and its own faces - Cardassians
and Klingons alongside Kraliens and Torgoth.

It could not be written under the old scheme for a reason worth keeping: the roster had to
be spelled in the mission's four stock names, so `kralien` was the NAME OF A SLOT that some
Trek faction was wearing. There was no way left to say "and also, actually, Kraliens".
